> The global movement against corruption. This is the English edition of transparency.org. The file follows the llmstxt.org convention and lists the site's content in a form that is cheap for agents to read.

## How to use this site

- Append `.md` to any page URL for a markdown version of it, e.g. `https://www.transparency.org/en/about.md`.
- The `.md` URLs are for machines. When linking a human to a page, drop the `.md`.
- Pages that render their content in the browser — the CPI, the GCB, country profiles, the NIS tracker, the Western Balkans and Turkey cases, laws and people — have no useful markdown version. Their `.md` URLs redirect to the HTML page, and they are listed below without the `.md` suffix, under headings marked (HTML only). Read those as HTML.
- Every entry is dated. `published` is the publication date, `updated` the last edit.
- Most lists below are capped at 25 entries per section, newest first. Reference sections link to their index page instead, and country profiles are listed in full, A–Z. The sitemap has every URL: https://www.transparency.org/en/sitemaps-1-sitemap.xml
- The site is published in eight languages; each has its own `llms.txt` under its own URL prefix.

